course: dictionary
lesson: 11541
title: Words for people who speak for others
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ambassador is someone who speaks for a group or a country. Look at the clues in this sentence: «The ambassador from France went to live in London to speak for her country.» She lives in another country and speaks for France there, so an ambassador is an important official who does this job.
explain: The word also works in everyday school life. «Our pupil ambassadors showed the visitors around the school.» Pupil ambassadors are not diplomats. They are children who represent their school and help other people. Ask yourself: who is doing the speaking or promoting, and for whom?
explain: The words around ambassador give you more clues. «Ambassador to» tells you which country, and «school ambassador» tells you it is about a school. Swap in your meaning, "a person who speaks for or promotes something," and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: An ambassador is an important official sent by one country to live in another country.
fact: An ambassador speaks for their own country while living abroad, and usually works from an embassy.
fact: Ambassador can also mean a person who represents or promotes something, such as a school ambassador.
fact: Phrases you may see include ambassador to (a country), goodwill ambassador, and brand ambassador.
exercise: «The ambassador from France went to live in London to speak for her country.» Who is the ambassador speaking for? | The people of London only | Her family back home | The visitors to the school | *Her own country, France
exercise: «Our pupil ambassadors showed the visitors around the school.» What are the pupil ambassadors doing? | Living in another country | Cleaning the classrooms after lunch | *Representing the school and helping visitors
exercise: Ella says, «I am the school's reading ambassador.» What does reading ambassador suggest? | A teacher who marks spelling tests | Someone who reads the most books in the library | A person who lives in another country | *Someone who promotes and encourages reading
test: «The ambassador to Japan works from the embassy in Tokyo.» Where does the ambassador usually work? | A bank in the city centre | A castle on the hill | A boarding school | *An embassy
test: «She is a goodwill ambassador for the charity, so she tells everyone about its work.» What does goodwill ambassador mean? | A person who runs a shop | *A person who promotes a cause in a friendly way | A person who sells tickets at the door | A person who guards a border
exam: Which word means an official who speaks for their country while living in another country? | *ambassador | pupil | tourist | visitor
